 "incidents": [
  "Drive uploads through rclone's shared client ID hit Google's rate limit (RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED); uploads were made best-effort with long retries and training never waited for them. All 8 full checkpoints of both runs reached Drive.",
  "Resume did not load weights: checkpoints store them as model.language_model.*, which Trainer's resume does not map, so it silently kept the untrained weights. Found in the smoke test (loss after resume differed by 0.03-0.045); fixed by loading the checkpoint with from_pretrained (difference <= 0.001 afterwards). The formal runs never resumed.",
  "colab exec with the cell fed on stdin hung in the background twice; those commands were killed before they ran and all later cells were run from files (-f).",
  "Restarting the kernel was not permitted, so the old orchestration could not be swapped for the background-upload version while the run was live; the end of each run waited for bf16 uploads.",
  "bf16 exports for 1k, 2k and 4k did not finish uploading to Drive (model.safetensors missing) because of the rate limit; generation used the exports on the VM. They can be re-exported from full/step_0025/0050/0100 with the export in run_formal.py (a deterministic cast; not re-checked against the lost files)."
 ],
